menu "Runtime Log Control"

config LOGCTL
	bool "Runtime log control support"
	default n
	depends on TASH
	---help---
		Enable runtime control of module logging via TASH commands.
		This allows enabling/disabling logs for specific modules at runtime
		without recompilation.

		By default, all modules are enabled at boot time based on compile-time
		CONFIG_DEBUG_* settings. Use TASH commands to dynamically control
		logging at runtime.

		TASH Commands:
		- logctl list: Show status of all modules
		- logctl enable <module>: Enable logging for a module
		- logctl disable <module>: Disable logging for a module
		- logctl enable_all: Enable all modules
		- logctl disable_all: Disable all modules

		Supported modules: common, audio, binfmt, fs, lib, mm, net, ble,
		smp, pm, sched, syscall, tash, wificsi, eventloop, media,
		preference, st_things, task_manager, and more.

endmenu
